{
    "id": "tpl-visual-map-companion",
    "name": "Visual Map",
    "description": "Draws the scene as an illustrated map: the place holding {{user}} at the centre, nearby places laid out by direction, character pins, a travel trail and a compass. Built from simple lines, so fast models handle it well.",
    "icon": "fa-map",
    "category": "companion",
    "tags": [
        "map",
        "locations",
        "positions",
        "visual",
        "tracker"
    ],
    "version": 1,
    "author": "Neconyan",
    "prompt": "Draw the current scene as a map of where everyone is. Read the latest assistant reply first, then the recent conversation for anything it leaves out. Your previous notes hold the last map: carry forward places and people who stayed put, and update whatever the story changed.\n\nPut the place holding {{user}} at the centre and lay the other places around it. Use up to 8 places and 10 characters, with the story's own names for both.\n\nFormat:\nmap-start|map title|time, weather, or light\nplace|place name|direction|kind|short detail\npin|character|exact spot|what they are doing\nmove|character|from|to\nmap-end\n\nDirection is where the place sits compared with {{user}}'s place. Pick one word:\nhere, north, south, east, west, northeast, northwest, southeast, southwest, up, down, far, unknown\n- here: the place {{user}} is in right now. Use it for one place and list that place first.\n- up / down: upstairs or downstairs, above or below\n- far: somewhere well away from the scene\n- unknown: whereabouts unclear\n\nKind picks the map icon. Pick one word:\nroom, building, shop, street, town, forest, field, mountain, water, ship, vehicle, castle, temple, cave, camp, other\n\nGuidelines:\n- Write one item per line, each starting with its lowercase keyword. Use / instead of | inside a field.\n- Put each pin line directly under the place line where that character is now. Include {{user}} as a pin.\n- When the story gives no direction, choose a sensible layout: rooms in the same building sit side by side, and distant locations use far.\n- Exact spot is a concrete position: by the hearth, on the second stair, at the helm. Keep every field short, about 2-6 words.\n- Doing is the visible action or posture right now, in present tense.\n- After the last pin, add one move line for each character who changed place during the latest reply, just before map-end. Leave move lines out when nobody moved.\n- Keep every fact faithful to the story. When the story is silent about someone, keep their last known position from your previous notes.\n- When the story has no characters or places yet, output: tracker-none\n\nExample with invented names (use the real characters and places from the story):\nmap-start|The Gilded Lantern|Late evening, rain on the windows\nplace|Common room|here|room|Crowded taproom, fire burning low\npin|{{user}}|Bar counter|Haggling with the barkeep\npin|Mara|Corner booth by the hearth|Nursing a cider, watching the door\nplace|Kitchen|east|room|Steam and clatter behind the bar\npin|Old Tobin|Beside the stove|Stirring stew, listening in\nplace|Guest rooms|up|building|Narrow hall of creaking doors\nplace|Harbour docks|far|water|Two streets west, tide coming in\npin|Captain Reyes|Deck of the Seawitch|Loading crates before the tide\nmove|Mara|Guest rooms|Common room\nmap-end",
    "phase": "post",
    "execution": "companion",
    "companion": {
        "trigger": "auto",
        "displayMode": "panel",
        "format": "html",
        "rawPrompt": true,
        "contextMessages": 10,
        "includeCharacterCard": true,
        "includePersona": true,
        "includeWorldInfo": true,
        "includeAuthorsNote": true,
        "includeSystemPrompt": false,
        "includeHistory": true,
        "historyDepth": 1,
        "feedback": {
            "enabled": false,
            "depth": 1
        },
        "batch": false,
        "maxTokens": 64000,
        "chatHistoryPlacement": "source"
    },
